# LeakSanitizer suppressions for `make fuzz`.
#
# iced-x86 builds its decoder tables once per process, in a lazy_static, and LeakSanitizer
# reports the opcode handlers it boxes there: 552 bytes in 12 allocations, the same whether a
# run takes one input or ten (measured with the writer_roundtrip target). It is third-party
# initialisation, not a leak an input causes; a leak that grows with the inputs is reported.
# A suppression matches a symbolized stack, so `make fuzz` sets ASAN_SYMBOLIZER_PATH.
leak:iced_x86::decoder::table_de
